# SemanticScript standard-library canonical module: standard.time.

# rationale: Canonical standard-library module for time helpers.
# invariant: The standard module entry is this file; tests live beside it as `main.test.sem`.
module standard.time
purpose module standard.time "Canonical standard-library module for time helpers."
moduleOwns standard.time "The official import path `standard.time` and this module's implementation body."
moduleDoesNotOwn standard.time "App-specific wrappers, compatibility aliases, or generated build artifacts."
invariant module standard.time "The standard module entry is this file; tests live beside it as `main.test.sem`."

exportConstant standard.time timeModuleVersionText
exportOperation standard.time readProcessCpuClockTicks
exportOperation standard.time readCurrentUnixEpochSeconds
exportOperation standard.time convertSecondsToWholeHours
exportOperation standard.time convertSecondsToWholeMinutes
exportOperation standard.time convertMinutesToSeconds
exportOperation standard.time convertHoursToSeconds
exportOperation standard.time convertUnixEpochSecondsToDays
exportOperation standard.time isGregorianLeapYear
storage module immutable timeModuleVersionText String "standard.time 0.1"

# Canonical standard-library implementation body.
# ============================================================
# SEMANTICSCRIPT STANDARD LIBRARY: <time.h>-style time operations
# ============================================================
#
# rationale: C's <time.h> exposes clock() / time() as floor
#   primitives and a flotilla of conversion macros for seconds /
#   minutes / hours / days. The refined surface drops Result X Void
#   from the total conversions, returns Bool from the predicate
#   isGregorianLeapYear, and keeps clock/time reads as real
#   operations with `effect read clock.realTime` declarations.
#
# invariant: every conversion is integer-division based; results
#   are floor-rounded toward negative infinity for non-negative
#   inputs (matching the LLVM sdiv semantics).
#
# security: clock / time reveal coarse-grained timing
#   information. Callers that handle secret-dependent data must
#   not branch on these values.
#
# timing: conversions are O(1). clock / time make one libc call.
#
# observability: the OS-time wrappers do not log themselves;
#   wrappers may.

# This is a pure-module (library) file: it exports operations
# consumed by other programs (notably std/time/main.test.sem which
# importModules it and runs the smoke). The project / target /
# runtime / entry block is retained so the module can still be
# linted standalone - the entry just points at the first exported
# operation rather than a `main` smoke.

# CPU-clock and wall-clock reads are observable side effects that
# need their own capability proofs; the time-slot allocation /
# release pair needs the heap capabilities. These remain in the
# impl module because impl operations (readProcessCpuClockTicks,
# readCurrentUnixEpochSeconds) declare `useCapability` against them.
capability clockCpuReadCapability clock.cpu read
capability clockRealTimeReadCapability clock.realTime read
capability heapAllocationCapability heap allocate
capability heapFreeCapability heap free

# Canonical conversion factors.
domainLiteral secondsPerMinuteValue Int64 60
domainLiteralTrust secondsPerMinuteValue trustedStaticLiteral
domainLiteral secondsPerHourValue Int64 3600
domainLiteralTrust secondsPerHourValue trustedStaticLiteral
domainLiteral secondsPerDayValue Int64 86400
domainLiteralTrust secondsPerDayValue trustedStaticLiteral

# Leap-year rule literals.
domainLiteral leapYearDivisorFour Int64 4
domainLiteralTrust leapYearDivisorFour trustedStaticLiteral
domainLiteral leapYearDivisorHundred Int64 100
domainLiteralTrust leapYearDivisorHundred trustedStaticLiteral
domainLiteral leapYearDivisorFourHundred Int64 400
domainLiteralTrust leapYearDivisorFourHundred trustedStaticLiteral
domainLiteral integerZeroBoundaryForTime Int64 0
domainLiteralTrust integerZeroBoundaryForTime trustedStaticLiteral
domainLiteral timeSlotByteSize ByteCount 8
domainLiteralTrust timeSlotByteSize trustedStaticLiteral

# section time.clockReaders

# rationale: Returns CPU clock ticks since the start of this process via libc clock(). Divide by CLOCKS_PER_SEC for seconds.
# invariant: Monotonically non-decreasing within a single process run.
# warning: Tick rate is platform-defined (CLOCKS_PER_SEC); do not compare across machines without conversion.
operation readProcessCpuClockTicks
output operation readProcessCpuClockTicks Int64
useCapability readProcessCpuClockTicks clockCpuReadCapability
effect readProcessCpuClockTicks read clock.cpu
memory readProcessCpuClockTicks heap no
async readProcessCpuClockTicks no
purpose operation readProcessCpuClockTicks "Returns CPU clock ticks since the start of this process via libc clock(). Divide by CLOCKS_PER_SEC for seconds."
invariant operation readProcessCpuClockTicks "Monotonically non-decreasing within a single process run."
warning readProcessCpuClockTicks "Tick rate is platform-defined (CLOCKS_PER_SEC); do not compare across machines without conversion."
guarantee readProcessCpuClockTicks "Always returns; never throws."
label startReadProcessCpuClockTicks
call libcClockCall c.clock
run libcClockCall
bind value cpuClockTickCount Int64 libcClockCall
return value cpuClockTickCount

# rationale: Returns seconds since 1970-01-01 00:00:00 UTC via libc time(). Returns 0 on allocation failure of the libc time_t* output slot.
# invariant: Monotonically non-decreasing per real-time clock; not guaranteed monotonic across clock adjustments.
# warning: Wall-clock value is subject to NTP adjustments / DST / manual changes; for monotonic intervals use readProcessCpuClockTicks. A 0 return indicates allocation failure, not a 1970-01-01 timestamp.
operation readCurrentUnixEpochSeconds
output operation readCurrentUnixEpochSeconds Int64
useCapability readCurrentUnixEpochSeconds clockRealTimeReadCapability
useCapability readCurrentUnixEpochSeconds heapAllocationCapability
useCapability readCurrentUnixEpochSeconds heapFreeCapability
effect readCurrentUnixEpochSeconds read clock.realTime
effect readCurrentUnixEpochSeconds allocate heap
effect readCurrentUnixEpochSeconds free heap
memory readCurrentUnixEpochSeconds heap yes
memoryAllocationSource readCurrentUnixEpochSeconds allocateTimeSlotCall
async readCurrentUnixEpochSeconds no
purpose operation readCurrentUnixEpochSeconds "Returns seconds since 1970-01-01 00:00:00 UTC via libc time(). Returns 0 on allocation failure of the libc time_t* output slot."
invariant operation readCurrentUnixEpochSeconds "Monotonically non-decreasing per real-time clock; not guaranteed monotonic across clock adjustments."
warning readCurrentUnixEpochSeconds "Wall-clock value is subject to NTP adjustments / DST / manual changes; for monotonic intervals use readProcessCpuClockTicks. A 0 return indicates allocation failure, not a 1970-01-01 timestamp."
guarantee readCurrentUnixEpochSeconds "Always returns; never throws."
# rationale: libc time() accepts a time_t* output parameter. We
#   allocate a single 8-byte slot, pass it in, ignore the slot
#   write, and use the function's return value. The slot is freed
#   via `defer` so any path through the function (including the
#   allocation-failure leg) leaves the heap clean. We absorb the
#   malloc failure as a 0 return rather than complicating the
#   output type with Result encoding - the compiler can't
#   distinguish a "value 0" Result.OK from a Result.Err variant
#   index 0 today, and unix time = 0 is a vanishingly rare value
#   (1970-01-01 UTC) callers can flag separately if needed.
label startReadCurrentUnixEpochSeconds
call allocateTimeSlotCall c.malloc
argument allocateTimeSlotCall size ByteCount timeSlotByteSize
run allocateTimeSlotCall
bind value timeSlotPointer OpaquePointer allocateTimeSlotCall
bind error timeSlotAllocationError Int32 allocateTimeSlotCall
branch error source allocateTimeSlotCall target timeSlotAllocationFailedHandler
defer releaseAllocateTimeSlotCall c.free timeSlotPointer
call libcTimeCall c.time
argument libcTimeCall slot OpaquePointer timeSlotPointer
run libcTimeCall
bind value currentUnixSeconds Int64 libcTimeCall
return value currentUnixSeconds

# Allocation-failure leg: c.malloc returned NULL. We surface the
# bound error value (the pointer-as-i32 NULL = 0) as the return -
# this both documents the failure cause in the IR via the
# bindError line above and produces the documented 0 sentinel
# (sign-extended from i32 to i64). We do NOT call c.free here
# because we never successfully allocated.
label timeSlotAllocationFailedHandler
return value timeSlotAllocationError

# section time.conversions

# rationale: Returns secondCount / 3600 - the number of whole hours represented.
# invariant: Floor-divides toward zero (LLVM sdiv) for non-negative inputs.
operation convertSecondsToWholeHours
input operation convertSecondsToWholeHours secondCount Int64
output operation convertSecondsToWholeHours Int64
memory convertSecondsToWholeHours heap no
async convertSecondsToWholeHours no
purpose operation convertSecondsToWholeHours "Returns secondCount / 3600 - the number of whole hours represented."
invariant operation convertSecondsToWholeHours "Floor-divides toward zero (LLVM sdiv) for non-negative inputs."
guarantee convertSecondsToWholeHours "Total."
label startConvertSecondsToWholeHours
call divideBySecondsPerHourCall math.divideInt64
argument divideBySecondsPerHourCall left Int64 secondCount
argument divideBySecondsPerHourCall right Int64 secondsPerHourValue
run divideBySecondsPerHourCall
bind value wholeHoursResult Int64 divideBySecondsPerHourCall
return value wholeHoursResult

# rationale: Returns secondCount / 60 - the number of whole minutes represented.
# invariant: Floor-divides toward zero.
operation convertSecondsToWholeMinutes
input operation convertSecondsToWholeMinutes secondCount Int64
output operation convertSecondsToWholeMinutes Int64
memory convertSecondsToWholeMinutes heap no
async convertSecondsToWholeMinutes no
purpose operation convertSecondsToWholeMinutes "Returns secondCount / 60 - the number of whole minutes represented."
invariant operation convertSecondsToWholeMinutes "Floor-divides toward zero."
guarantee convertSecondsToWholeMinutes "Total."
label startConvertSecondsToWholeMinutes
call divideBySecondsPerMinuteCall math.divideInt64
argument divideBySecondsPerMinuteCall left Int64 secondCount
argument divideBySecondsPerMinuteCall right Int64 secondsPerMinuteValue
run divideBySecondsPerMinuteCall
bind value wholeMinutesResult Int64 divideBySecondsPerMinuteCall
return value wholeMinutesResult

# rationale: Returns minuteCount * 60 seconds.
# invariant: Result wraps under multiplication overflow at Int64.
operation convertMinutesToSeconds
input operation convertMinutesToSeconds minuteCount Int64
output operation convertMinutesToSeconds Int64
memory convertMinutesToSeconds heap no
async convertMinutesToSeconds no
purpose operation convertMinutesToSeconds "Returns minuteCount * 60 seconds."
invariant operation convertMinutesToSeconds "Result wraps under multiplication overflow at Int64."
guarantee convertMinutesToSeconds "Total."
label startConvertMinutesToSeconds
call multiplyMinutesBySixtyCall math.multiplyInt64
argument multiplyMinutesBySixtyCall left Int64 minuteCount
argument multiplyMinutesBySixtyCall right Int64 secondsPerMinuteValue
run multiplyMinutesBySixtyCall
bind value secondsFromMinutesResult Int64 multiplyMinutesBySixtyCall
return value secondsFromMinutesResult

# rationale: Returns hourCount * 3600 seconds.
# invariant: Result wraps under overflow.
operation convertHoursToSeconds
input operation convertHoursToSeconds hourCount Int64
output operation convertHoursToSeconds Int64
memory convertHoursToSeconds heap no
async convertHoursToSeconds no
purpose operation convertHoursToSeconds "Returns hourCount * 3600 seconds."
invariant operation convertHoursToSeconds "Result wraps under overflow."
guarantee convertHoursToSeconds "Total."
label startConvertHoursToSeconds
call multiplyHoursBy3600Call math.multiplyInt64
argument multiplyHoursBy3600Call left Int64 hourCount
argument multiplyHoursBy3600Call right Int64 secondsPerHourValue
run multiplyHoursBy3600Call
bind value secondsFromHoursResult Int64 multiplyHoursBy3600Call
return value secondsFromHoursResult

# rationale: Returns whole days since 1970-01-01 from an epoch-seconds value.
# invariant: Floor-divides toward zero.
operation convertUnixEpochSecondsToDays
input operation convertUnixEpochSecondsToDays epochSecondCount Int64
output operation convertUnixEpochSecondsToDays Int64
memory convertUnixEpochSecondsToDays heap no
async convertUnixEpochSecondsToDays no
purpose operation convertUnixEpochSecondsToDays "Returns whole days since 1970-01-01 from an epoch-seconds value."
invariant operation convertUnixEpochSecondsToDays "Floor-divides toward zero."
guarantee convertUnixEpochSecondsToDays "Total."
label startConvertUnixEpochSecondsToDays
call divideBySecondsPerDayCall math.divideInt64
argument divideBySecondsPerDayCall left Int64 epochSecondCount
argument divideBySecondsPerDayCall right Int64 secondsPerDayValue
run divideBySecondsPerDayCall
bind value daysSinceEpochResult Int64 divideBySecondsPerDayCall
return value daysSinceEpochResult

# section time.calendar

# rationale: Returns true when candidateYear is a Gregorian leap year (divisible by 4 AND (not divisible by 100 OR divisible by 400)).
# invariant: Pure function of candidateYear; result depends only on the year value.
operation isGregorianLeapYear
input operation isGregorianLeapYear candidateYear Int64
output operation isGregorianLeapYear Bool
memory isGregorianLeapYear heap no
async isGregorianLeapYear no
purpose operation isGregorianLeapYear "Returns true when candidateYear is a Gregorian leap year (divisible by 4 AND (not divisible by 100 OR divisible by 400))."
invariant operation isGregorianLeapYear "Pure function of candidateYear; result depends only on the year value."
guarantee isGregorianLeapYear "Total."
# rationale: Gregorian leap-year rule per ISO 8601. The trichotomy
#   below short-circuits at the cheapest divisor first (4), then
#   400 (skipping the 100 check when divisible by 400), then 100.
label startIsGregorianLeapYear
call computeYearModuloFourCall math.moduloInt64
argument computeYearModuloFourCall left Int64 candidateYear
argument computeYearModuloFourCall right Int64 leapYearDivisorFour
run computeYearModuloFourCall
bind value yearModuloFour Int64 computeYearModuloFourCall
call detectNotDivisibleByFourCall math.notEqualInt64
argument detectNotDivisibleByFourCall left Int64 yearModuloFour
argument detectNotDivisibleByFourCall right Int64 integerZeroBoundaryForTime
run detectNotDivisibleByFourCall
bind value yearNotDivisibleByFour Bool detectNotDivisibleByFourCall
branch if condition yearNotDivisibleByFour target returnNotLeapYear
call computeYearModuloFourHundredCall math.moduloInt64
argument computeYearModuloFourHundredCall left Int64 candidateYear
argument computeYearModuloFourHundredCall right Int64 leapYearDivisorFourHundred
run computeYearModuloFourHundredCall
bind value yearModuloFourHundred Int64 computeYearModuloFourHundredCall
call detectDivisibleByFourHundredCall math.equalInt64
argument detectDivisibleByFourHundredCall left Int64 yearModuloFourHundred
argument detectDivisibleByFourHundredCall right Int64 integerZeroBoundaryForTime
run detectDivisibleByFourHundredCall
bind value yearDivisibleByFourHundred Bool detectDivisibleByFourHundredCall
branch if condition yearDivisibleByFourHundred target returnIsLeapYear
call computeYearModuloHundredCall math.moduloInt64
argument computeYearModuloHundredCall left Int64 candidateYear
argument computeYearModuloHundredCall right Int64 leapYearDivisorHundred
run computeYearModuloHundredCall
bind value yearModuloHundred Int64 computeYearModuloHundredCall
call detectDivisibleByHundredCall math.equalInt64
argument detectDivisibleByHundredCall left Int64 yearModuloHundred
argument detectDivisibleByHundredCall right Int64 integerZeroBoundaryForTime
run detectDivisibleByHundredCall
bind value yearDivisibleByHundred Bool detectDivisibleByHundredCall
branch if condition yearDivisibleByHundred target returnNotLeapYear
branch else target returnIsLeapYear
label returnIsLeapYear
storage module immutable isLeapYearTrue Bool true
return value isLeapYearTrue
label returnNotLeapYear
storage module immutable isLeapYearFalse Bool false
return value isLeapYearFalse
